00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
since elden ring launched back in  february of this year i have been  attempting to understand the story just  like everybody else i felt like i was  ready to make meaningful and stylish  content with a game that i was very much  looking forward to before the game was  released i wasn't sure how the game  would be received by the mainstream  audience i definitely noticed a very  clear effort by the marketing team of  elden ring that i had not seen before  from any prior release by from software  it felt like everyone knew about elden  ring and even players who had not played  a souls game before would be willing to  try this game just from the hype that  had been generating up to the release i  had thousands of hours under my belt  playing the previous titles by from  software and i felt ready to hit the  ground running with eldon ring to maybe  have a head start on understanding the  plotline and sequence of events that  took place leading up to our journey  through the lands between and i felt  like i did that for the most part  although somehow two of my most  successful videos are one with me just  walking around and asking questions for  six minutes and the other one is me  talking about how awesome radon is and  ever since i've been making videos on my  interpretation of the lore in elden ring  in most of these videos i'm extremely  proud of how they turned out as i  thought they were visually interesting  to watch with an emphasis on simplifying  my explanations on the subject so more  people can understand the story i  thought that researching and making  videos on streamlined subjects within  the lore would help me eventually  understand the overall storyline so i  could get better and better at making  these videos however i can say after  hundreds of hours of playing and  researching the ins and outs of almost  everything this game has to offer i am  now more confused than i was halfway  through my first playthrough i don't  feel confident in almost anything i  write in a script because there's likely  something within the game that  contradicts or devalues that subject to  put it simply trying to master the  understanding of the lore is frustrating  and my flame of ambition to make lore  videos on elden ring has been fading  recently but i won't dare go hollow on  you guys i will continue to thoroughly  research and play the game to hopefully  regain that flame once again that's what  you've all subscribed to this channel  for and i appreciate the support more  than you all could understand what i'm  trying to say is that i need to vent  this frustration out into the air so i  can simply just get over it and get back  to making good videos again i know that  i'm not the only one frustrated with the  story of elden ring and i do understand  that from software stories are meant to  be vague however when it came to the  souls series and bloodborne i at least  felt confident in my findings and  understanding of the story as a whole  however when it comes to elden ring i  sometimes feel like i'm personally being  told or shown something not to help with  the betterment of my understanding of  things but just for the sake of  confusing me further and nothing more  maybe this means i'm just not capable of  understanding a complicated story like  with elden ring i most of the time feel  like an unhinged detective functioning  only off of high amounts of caffeine and  i feel like most of the community acts  and feels this way as well creating  random speculations that just don't have  a ton of evidence supporting those  claims which in turn creates mass  confusion amongst the community at large  but with a game of this magnitude with a  massive interest in trying to figure out  all of this stuff by everybody in the  community this is just bound to happen  it's like when the police are trying to  catch an escaped felon for example and  they use the help of the community to  catch this criminal so they announce  that the felon is wearing a blue shirt  jeans and is in a white van then they  just get spammed with calls all over the  place for every white van that is seen  on the highway and every person wearing  a blue shirt and jeans do you see where  i'm going with this it just creates mass  confusion so you have to go digging  through all of that information to maybe  find something that can actually be seen  as logical or helpful and there are  almost endless examples within the game  of what i'm trying to convey here you  could point out any character boss event  quest line item description anything and  it will turn into a rabbit hole of  unhinged discussion on the true meaning  of any and all of those things and  convincing arguments can be made about  one side or the other with any and all  of those things as well there's so much  compelling information within this game  that it's possible to link quite  literally anything in the game with  something else while at the same time  also just not giving enough information  to make concrete theories with those  comparisons and this leads to random  confusion about basic concepts within  the game's lore which just destroys my  confidence with any clue i find when  researching and playing i suppose what  i'm truly afraid of is creating mundane  videos and content for you guys as i  stagnate with my understanding of eldon  ring's lore i don't want to make a video  that is based on an unhinged theory that  the game is almost seemingly designed  for which is just random bunches of  information that may or may not be  logical with the other beams within the  game's lore and i guess a question that  i should be asking myself is that does  it really need to make sense from  software is well aware that their  dedicated fan base is going to go down  every nook and cranny to uncover the  secrets that their game has to offer  it's a huge part of why their games have  had continued longevity over the years  and have developed such a strong fan  base because most people don't  understand the mysteries of the game  because of the extremely vague  storytelling so it's up to the community  to piece everything together to form a  coherent plot line for everyone to try  and understand new discoveries are made  years after release of all of these  games as there seems to be no end to the  secrets that these games offer and  that's exactly what from software once  they want their player base to continue  to try and understand the game which  makes them keep playing the game and  honestly there is nothing wrong with  from software doing that and at the end  of the day i just want to make good  content for you all to enjoy but the  more i play the game the more i've been  struggling to do so and this isn't  because of a lack of content like i've  been explaining there's seemingly  endless amounts of rabbit holes that we  could go down and discuss endless  comparisons of main themes that we could  speculate on and trying to convey those  themes in a meaningful and  understandable way has not only proven  to be difficult but in some ways feels  almost impossible it's like you have to  pick a side when interpreting the lore  or you'll find yourself helplessly  frustrated in confusion like i am  currently i don't like picking sides  when it comes to this i want to read  both sides of the story so i can truly  understand what it's meant to be but  when both sides of the coin are only  trying to disvalue the other through  confusion instead of logic you come out  with only frustration instead of  understanding and like i said earlier  maybe i'm just not capable of truly  understanding the lore in this game the  more i try to understand the more i just  get confused which wasn't the case with  me with any other from software game  i've played while the storytelling was  still vague with enough research the  lore of dark souls and bloodborne and  sakiro could be easily understood elden  ring is clearly the biggest game that  from software has ever developed and  they even got outside help from george  rr martin to assist in the creation of  the base world and its storyline it's  really not clear exactly what he helped  with but it seems like he was only there  in early development and nothing more  it's possible that the developers had to  change some things around throughout  development that just didn't make sense  with what george created for them and  this adds to my point the story of elden  ring feels like it was written by two  different writers that weren't on the  same page whatsoever this is the  constant feeling i have while trying to  understand elden ring but maybe i'm just  not being patient enough with elden ring  most of the time with from software the  storyline isn't truly understood or  expanded on until dlc releases and the  dlc is most of the time the best parts  of the game overall i believe dlc will  only help with my understanding of eldon  ring's lore because usually the dlcs are  more streamlined experiences with an  open world like elden ring it's easy to  get overwhelmed with everything that  you're finding but we are more than  likely going to get a somewhat linear  experience when dlc releases for elden  ring and with a more linear experience  we'll get information in a more linear  fashion so it'll be easier to link  things together in this way that's  pretty much what i'm looking for at this  point in eldon ring's lifespan and again  maybe that's just because i'm too stupid  or it's because we just aren't meant to  understand the storyline yet maybe it's  just because i personally prefer the  more linear aspects of from software's  previous titles and i'm just not used to  this new style of souls game yet i have  to be able to adapt to something new or  i won't be able to truly understand the  world that i'm playing in finally i want  to make clear that my frustration here  is my own fault i still believe that  eldon ring is a masterpiece that will  more than likely win game of the year  depending on how good god of war  ragnarok turns out to be but regardless  of that we'll probably be talking about  elden ring for years to come it is the  greatest success that from software has  ever had and it would be stupid to think  that they aren't working on dlc right  now to expand our understanding of a  world they clearly worked tirelessly on  for all of us to experience i am  frustrated with this game not for a lack  of effort by the developers but more of  a frustration with myself because all i  want to do is make meaningful  entertaining content for you all to  enjoy so that you don't have to go  through these frustrations yourself and  i will get over these frustrations and  the lore videos i'm currently working on  are some of the best i've ever made with  more of an emphasis on the cinematic  visuals of quest lines to better  illustrate the narrative for you guys so  don't for a second think i'm not gonna  keep trying because i love elden ring  too much to be able to give up on it i  just needed to get this out in the air  so i could move on and focus on making  the content i know i'm capable of making  maybe this was better to talk to a  therapist about but i felt the need to  make this video because you are the ones  who support the content your feedback is  how i make all future videos better so i  very much value the input of those that  watch it so thank you all for watching  to the end if you did make it to the end  of this video without leaving an angry  comment on how my frustrations are just  stupid then type bananafoot in the  comments so i know who the real ones are  why bananafoot i don't know i just think  the word is funny if you want to watch  all future lore videos early with no ads  whatsoever you can join my patreon for  as little as three dollars to receive  early access there's also multiple tiers  depending on how much you want to  support thank you to the ones that  already do and thank you again for  watching i will see you all in the next  lore video  take care  [Music]  you

